# LnShelf — .gitignore
# Kept deliberately short: this repo holds a .NET solution, a Blazor WASM
# client, and a compose file. Migrations under Features/**/Migrations are
# source and are committed — never ignore them.

# ---- Build output ----
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
publish/
*.binlog
msbuild.log

# ---- Test & benchmark output ----
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
*.coverage
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# ---- NuGet ----
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
packages/

# ---- Local config & secrets ----
# Secrets live in user-secrets locally and environment variables in the
# container (CLAUDE.md). Nothing secret belongs in appsettings.json, so
# appsettings.json / appsettings.Development.json stay committed — these
# patterns are the escape hatch for machine-local overrides only.
*.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docker-compose.override.yml

# ---- Local container data ----
# Compose uses named volumes (feature-spec §9); this covers ad-hoc bind mounts
# for Postgres, MinIO, or a local-disk ICoverStore implementation.
.data/

# ---- Personal data dropped in the repo during import work ----
# StoryGraph exports are real reading history — never commit them. Test
# fixtures live in Fixtures/ folders inside the test project and are deeper
# than root, so this root-only pattern leaves them alone.
/*.csv

# ---- IDE & editor ----
.vs/
.idea/
.fleet/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.DotSettings.user

# ---- Claude Code ----
# CLAUDE.md and .claude/rules/ are checked in — the local permission file is
# machine-specific, and the agent harness's scratch worktrees are whole copies
# of this repo that must never end up inside it.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# ---- OS junk ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
